<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand National Assembly of Turkey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Grand National Assembly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand National Assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> was opened by nationalist deputies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> on 23 April 1920, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in the name of the nation under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a>. Its government won the War of Independence, abolished the Ottoman sultanate in 1922 and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a> in 1923. It remains Turkey's parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey.jpg" alt="Grand National Assembly of Turkey" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juris Tiltins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_Turkish_Parliament_(T%C3%BCrkiye_B%C3%BCy%C3%BCk_Millet_Meclisi).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
